## One page per subsystem

Each runtime page under `docs/runtime/` answers:

| Section | Question |
| --- | --- |
| **Authority** | Who owns truth? |
| **Runtime** | What is the production path? |
| **Baseline** | What did good look like? (link) |
| **Known defects** | Missing capabilities ≠ instability |
| **Observation gate** | What must pass before evolution? |

Not 100 pages. **One place where reality is written down.**

Planned: payments · scheduling · communications · identity · inspection · pricing.

---

## Anti-ceremony

If a runtime document isn't helping someone make a decision in six months — **delete or rewrite it.**

The value is not having documentation. The value is **one authoritative page that matches the floor.**
